An error loaded from a struct field holds what the reachable program stores to
that field. Here nothing does, but the Target is not reachable from main or
init: its callers, which the analysis does not see, may write the field, so
the load stays unresolved(memory).
-- args --
a.go:@f
-- stdout --
$WORK/a.go:5:12-13: Error Set of example.com/fx.F: 1 entries, 1 unresolved
$WORK/a.go:6:9-14: unresolved(memory): field err of example.com/fx.S may be written by code that is not reachable from the Query's roots
	path (origin → target):
		$WORK/a.go:6:9-14: in example.com/fx.F
-- stderr --
errtrace: warning: target not reachable from main/init; parameters may lack candidates
-- go.mod --
module example.com/fx

go 1.24
-- a.go --
package fx

type S struct{ err error }

func /*@f*/F(s *S) error {
	return s.err
}
